==========================================================================
A. NO-RETURN IS NOT MULTIPLICATIVE -- the N times N* machine
==========================================================================
  THM-3001: reversal negates the circuit.  THM-3003 sec 1: a SYMMETRIC
  log-root measure forces R_k = R_(D-k), an antipalindromic circuit.
  The root multiset of N*N* is {r} union {1/r}, whose log-root measure is
  symmetric about 0 BY CONSTRUCTION.  So for every N, the product of the
  two ratio-monotone polynomials N and N* is ratio-PALINDROMIC, hence not
  monotone unless its circuit vanishes identically.

  The ANTIPALINDROME is universal (it needs no hypothesis on N).  Whether
  BOTH FACTORS are monotone is an extra property of the chosen N, and is
  what turns the identity into a counterexample to multiplicativity.
  machine applied to several N (A = N, B = N* up to scaling):
    N = (n+1)^2(n+2)       c(N)=-        c(N*)=+        c(N N*)=--++           antipalindrome=True product monotone=False  [counterexample]
    N = (n+1)^3(n+5)       c(N)=--       c(N*)=++       c(N N*)=---+++         antipalindrome=True product monotone=False  [counterexample]
    N = (n+1)(n+2)(n+7)    c(N)=-        c(N*)=+        c(N N*)=--++           antipalindrome=True product monotone=False  [counterexample]
    N = (n+2)^2(n+9)^3     c(N)=++-      c(N*)=+--      c(N N*)=++++----       antipalindrome=True product monotone=False  [factors not both monotone (identity still holds)]

  MINIMAL INTEGER WITNESS (exhaustive over integer roots <=6, degree <=5 each):
    total degree 6:  A roots ['1', '1', '2'],  B roots ['1', '2', '2']
      c(A)   = -   monotone=True
      c(B)   = +   monotone=True
      c(A*B) = ++--   monotone=False
    B is exactly A's reversal up to scaling (A roots {1,1,2}, reciprocals
    {1,1,1/2} = (1/2){2,2,1} = B roots), so this is the machine at its
    smallest, not a sporadic coincidence.
  VERDICT A: NOT CLOSED UNDER MULTIPLICATION (proved + minimal witness)

==========================================================================
B. THE FIRST-GAP WALL IS ITSELF RATIO-MONOTONE
==========================================================================
   M   deg(W)  distinct scales  sign changes  monotone   C(mu_W)     C(mu_W*)   C>=0>=C*
    6     129         7              0        True     +0.137011   -2.974661   True
    8     178         9              0        True     +0.151536   -4.730729   True
   10     229        11              0        True     +0.165714   -6.626403   True
   12     281        13              0        True     +0.178905   -8.720673   True
   14     330        15              0        True     +0.193836  -10.926369   True
  The wall's circuit is strictly POSITIVE throughout: zero reversals at
  degree 330.  THM-3001's necessary condition holds with a margin that
  GROWS in M on both sides.  The wall is not the obstruction.
  VERDICT B: WALL IS MONOTONE AND CLEARS THE NECESSARY CONDITION

==========================================================================
C. DICHOTOMY: separation, not root count, creates reversals
==========================================================================
  same number of distinct scales, two extremes:
    near-continuum (the wall, M=10): 11 distinct scales spread over
      [1/2, 10] with ratios -> 1 :  sign changes = 0
    well separated: 11 distinct scales with ratio 10^6 :  sign changes = 19  (2m-3 = 19)
  Same scale COUNT, opposite behaviour.  THM-3004's cluster law needs
  separation; a near-continuum root measure sits at the other extreme with
  no reversals at all.

==========================================================================
SUMMARY  non-multiplicative=True  wall-monotone=True  dichotomy=True
==========================================================================
